Subject: [PATCH] iommu/qcom: log faults rejected by the client handler

report_iommu_fault() returns zero when handled and a negative error when
unhandled. The inverted check hides display faults: the MSM display path
returns -ENOSYS after requesting a register snapshot. Report those faults
with the existing rate limit.

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -200,7 +200,7 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_iommu_fault(int irq, void *dev)
 	fsynr = iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FSYNR0);
 	iova = iommu_readq(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FAR);
 
-	if (!report_iommu_fault(ctx->domain, ctx->dev, iova, 0)) {
+	if (report_iommu_fault(ctx->domain, ctx->dev, iova, 0)) {
 		dev_err_ratelimited(ctx->dev,
 				    "Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x%x, "
 				    "iova=0x%016llx, fsynr=0x%x, cb=%d\n",
